DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T210000
SUMMARY:Weekly Game Night at Blue Note
DESCRIPTION:Yolo County Board Game Gathering\nUpdate 8/14/25:\n**We're sti
 ll active**\, but we primarily use Discord to chat and plan events. (See g
 roup description for invite link.)\n\nWe still meet every Wednesday for bo
 ard games at Blue Note Brewing Company. We'll have a handful of tables res
 erved near the back\; just look for the pile of board games.\n\nPeople usu
 ally start arriving around 5pm\, and games start whenever people are ready
 . Blue Note closes at 9pm\, and although we have a 5-10 minute grace perio
 d there\, you should be in the process of final scoring by 9\, or else pac
 k it up and play again another day.\n\nGame night is open to all ages! Blu
 e Note is a brewery\, not a bar\, so there's no restriction against minors
 . In addition to their crafted-in-house beer selection\, water and sodas a
 re available.\n\nYou're not required to buy anything in order to join us\,
  but we do encourage you to support local businesses. Blue Note's chef tea
 m makes a mean pizza\, and there are other nearby downtown restaurants and
  businesses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/yolo-county-board-game-gathering/even
 ts/316904500/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261009T001804Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261009T001804Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"UC Davis Library": "https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/savor-fresh-starts"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ucdavis_library
SUMMARY:Savor: Fresh Starts: How California Farmers Markets Changed the Wa
 y We Eat
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T193000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54189112758119
DESCRIPTION:Join us for this quarter's Savor event: Fresh Starts: How Cali
 fornia Farmers Markets Changed the Way We Eat.\n \n\nThe formation of the 
 Davis Farmers Market 50 years ago was a revolutionary movement to connect 
 consumers directly to farmers and helped shape the fresh flavors of Califo
 rnia cuisine. Markets have been a cornerstone of the community and have al
 so played a pivotal role in food access\, especially during supply chain s
 hortages and widespread food recalls. Inevitably\, markets have evolved. J
 oin us as we explore the history\, impact and changing role of farmers mar
 kets in local communities. \n\nThe event will feature a panel of leading i
 ndustry experts including:\n \n\nAnn Evans\, UC Davis alumna\, co-founder 
 of the Davis Farmers Market and Davis Food Co-op\, author and former mayor
  and city council member of the City of DavisSam Greenlee\, chief executiv
 e officer of Alchemist Community Development CorporationChutharat Sae Tong
 \, co-owner of Majka Pizzeria and Bakery in SacramentoModerator Catherine 
 Brinkley\, associate professor in Human Ecology\, Community and Regional D
 evelopment at UC Davis \n\nA pop-up exhibit from the library's Archives an
 d Special Collections will be on display.\n\n \n\nThe event includes a wel
 come reception\, a hosted bar and appetizers. Tickets are $25/person ($15/
 students). \n\n \n\nThe Savor lecture series is a collaboration between th
 e Robert Mondavi Institute for Wine and Food Science and the UC Davis Libr
 ary.
LOCATION:Robert Mondavi Institute - Sensory Building\, Sensory Theater
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/savor-fresh-starts
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
